# MLB-95 public-repo hardening (2026-07-21):
# - raw league archives were untracked but NOT ignored -- one `git add .`
#   away from a very bad day
# - the golden corpora are rendered from the real league (owner names
#   throughout), so they live locally + on the private dev remote only
# - the trade-intel handoff must never be committed anywhere
data/
tests/fixtures/almanac_v1_1_0/
tests/fixtures/cbs_almanac/
tests/fixtures/baseline_summary_current.txt
tests/fixtures/baseline_records_report.txt
Trade Intel API Handoff.md

# Working drafts of the portfolio README (2026-07-28). The finished
# rewrite is README.md; these are the review copies that fed it and
# they should never reach the public repo. README_DRAFT.md was tracked
# by mistake and is untracked in the same commit -- the file stays on
# disk, it just stops being published.
README_DRAFT.md
README-merged-draft*.md

# Screenshot working folder (MLB-100). Raw capture frames land here
# unvetted -- some carry real owner names straight off the live sheet.
# Only frames that have been eyeballed and curated get committed, and
# they go to docs/img/ under a kebab-case name. Both spellings, so a
# case-sensitive checkout cannot sneak the folder back in.
Screenshots/
screenshots/
